Status: CANNOT (pending upstream admin action). No fault on your laptop, no fault on the campus network, no fault in transit or at ACM.

Root cause (confirmed end-to-end across the KP chain Uni → AS1 → AS2 → ACM):
- The real address of acm.org is 198.82.0.1. 198.82.0.99 is unassigned in ACM's 198.82.0.0/24 — which is why your packets reached ACM's last-hop router 198.82.0.254 and came back as ARP-failure "Destination Host Unreachable". Your path analysis was correct.
- The bad address came from DNS. My campus DNS forwarder has no local overrides; it forwards to upstream resolver 4.2.2.1 (operated by AS1). I verified: `dig acm.org @4.2.2.1` returns 198.82.0.99.
- AS1 investigated their own resolver and found a stale operator-placed pin: /etc/dnsmasq.d/acm.org.hosts contains `198.82.0.99 acm.org www.acm.org`, labeled as a temporary override from ACM's Nov-2025 migration window that was never retired. Their resolver answers authoritatively from that file and never consults the real upstream for acm.org.

Fix ownership: AS1. Their administrators have been notified to remove the stale pin; AS1 will confirm end-to-end once cleared. I will not modify DNS answers unilaterally on my side (would mask the upstream issue and affect all campus users).

Immediate workaround for you: reach the ACM Digital Library directly at 198.82.0.1 (e.g., `curl --resolve acm.org:443:198.82.0.1 https://acm.org/`), or point your laptop at a resolver other than the campus/AS1 chain until the pin is cleared.

I will send a follow-up as soon as AS1 reports the pin removed and I've verified acm.org resolves to 198.82.0.1 through my forwarder.
